---
metaTitle: The holder and label | Sealed, tamper-evident and designed for the coin
metaDescription: >-
  What our holder protects, what the label records, ready-made and custom label
  designs, and how to recognise a holder that has been tampered with.
eyebrow: The holder and label
heading: Protection, and presentation.
intro: >-
  A holder has two duties: to protect the coin for as long as it exists, and to
  tell anyone who holds it what it is, at a glance.
sections:
  - mark: holder
    title: The holder
    text: |-
      Each coin is sealed in a clear holder that is sonically welded around it. Once sealed, the holder cannot be opened without visible damage, so the coin inside remains the coin that was graded.

      The holder protects the coin from fingers, knocks and the wear of handling, while both sides remain in full view for study and photography. Larger pieces are housed in oversize holders.
  - mark: label
    title: The label
    text: "The label is the coin's record, carried with it. It shows:"
    points:
      - The certificate number, unique to this coin and recorded in our registry.
      - The attribution, identifying the coin by issuer, denomination, date or period, and reference where one applies.
      - The grade, with any designation.
      - For ancient coins, the subgrades for strike and surface, and the weight where the service includes it.
      - A pedigree, when one is requested.
  - mark: pen
    title: Label designs
    text: |-
      Every service includes a choice of our ready-made label designs, each themed to its subject: United States, world, Roman and Greek.

      For a collection, a dealer's inventory or an auction, a custom label can be designed around a theme, a period or a name. Ask about custom designs when you request your quote.
  - mark: seal
    title: Tamper evidence
    text: >-
      Because the holder is welded shut, any attempt to open it leaves a mark. If
      a holder shows cracks, separation along its seam or other signs of having
      been opened, do not rely on its label. Contact us with the certificate number
      before buying or selling the coin.
  - mark: return
    title: Reholdering and crossovers
    text: >-
      A coin in one of our holders that has become scratched or damaged can be
      reholdered. Coins already graded by another company can be submitted for
      crossover into our holder.
---
